# Battle-Tested Alignment & Resolution Fix

## Goal
Resolve the `UnableToResolveError: expo-linking` crash and eliminate remaining dependency warnings to achieve a 100% green launch. 

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE]
> **Minimalist Fix:**
> Instead of installing new packages (respecting your instruction), I will swap `expo-linking` for the built-in [react-native](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/node_modules/.bin/react-native) Linking module. This solves the crash without adding bloat.
>
> **Version Alignment:**
> I am aligning `@types/react` and `react-native-worklets` to the versions specifically requested by your terminal output to remove the last remaining warnings.

## Proposed Changes

### [gurudevi-mobile]

#### [MODIFY] [LibraryScreen.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/src/screens/LibraryScreen.tsx)
- Change `import * as Linking from 'expo-linking'` to `import { Linking } from 'react-native'`.
- Remove `import { useRouter } from 'expo-router'`.

#### [MODIFY] [package.json](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/package.json)
- Pin `react-native-worklets` to `0.5.1` (matching terminal request).

### [Monorepo Root]

